#!/usr/bin/env bash

codex exec << "EOF"
1. Move the alphabet history page ahead of the TOC in master.tex
2. Move the Regular and Bold sections on the source key to the
    next page, so the source key starts with J.
3. make R's text color be the same as P's, and make R's background
   be slightly darker or more transparent in dark mode. Ideally,
   do this by mixing the page's bg color with R's bg color by some
   amount.
4. In the footnote in 01-genesis/01.tex that says:

    Translator’s Aside: The abruptness of the reading at this point has led many commentators to posit a lacuna in
    the text; still others have suggested it may be a haplography, or any of a number of other scholarly ways of saying
    something’s missing.

    Make that footnote be a \\hangingfootnote so the indents are
    more like python indents and less like book indents.

5. Remove the background from the Deuteronomistic sources,
   put preserve the current lines by just commenting them out.

6. Move the 'Whatcha doing? Ah!' between Gen 2:10 and Gen 2:11
   over to the right of the page so it's under the Benaiah
   table (right aligned, I mean.)

7. Add some placeholder dialogue in my style after that where
   the A character says to the B character something like
   Sorry, you startled me. I was pretty deep down a rabbit hole there.
   Then A should say to B something like I think I could use
   someone else around to keep me from going off the rails.
   I've been trying to cut back. B says cut back on what?
   A says On bible. I'm addicted. It's becoming a problem.
   B agrees to stick around, but says I'm not sure if I'll
   be able to help. I don't really understand this stuff.
   A says that's good. It'll force me to keep it simple.
   Then B says can we back up a line or two? I didn't really
   understand that last one. Then we proceed to Gen 2:11 in
   the next line where A says no one knows what Pishon means.
   Then they resume on the next line

Do all that now, and make it perfect.
EOF
